# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
backend/venv/

# Secrets
.env

# Generated/cached AI-layer data (regenerable from source, not curated
# content): the Chroma vector store is rebuilt by ai/tools/build_kb.py and
# the ATT&CK bundle is re-downloaded on demand by app/mitre/loader.py.
ai/vector_store/
ai/mitre/*.json

# Generated by ai/tools/hallucination_spot_check.py and
# llm_cost_latency_check.py -- raw per-run output, not curated content.
# Findings are written up by hand in docs/ARCHITECTURE.md instead.
ai/tools/*_output.json

# Frontend (Day 14) -- frontend/.gitignore covers this locally too, but keep
# the root aware for `git status` run from the repo root.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/

# Real (not synthetic) clean-corpus captures from a contributor's own PC
# (backend/scripts/run_detection_benchmark.py, build_failure_matrix.py) --
# these carry the owner's real Windows username/hostname baked into the
# EVTX records, so they stay local rather than being committed. Neither
# script requires them to be present; a fresh clone just has fewer clean
# fixtures to test false positives against.
backend/sample_logs/real_world_fixtures/benign/
# ML layer: regenerable intermediates, not curated inputs.
# - cache/ holds pickled normalized events, rebuilt by run_detection_benchmark.py
# The trained model (app/ml/models/anomaly_detector.joblib) IS tracked: the
# ingest path needs it at runtime, and a fresh clone without it silently has
# no ML layer at all.
backend/scripts/cache/
